## Soft Delete Pattern

**Never hard delete. Mark as deleted instead.**

```python
# ✅ CORRECT: Soft delete
async def delete(self, tenant_id: UUID, material_id: UUID) -> None:
    stmt = select(MaterialModel).where(
        MaterialModel.tenant_id == tenant_id,
        MaterialModel.id == material_id,
        MaterialModel.is_deleted == False
    )
    result = await session.execute(stmt)
    material = result.scalars().first()
    
    if material:
        material.is_deleted = True
        material.deleted_at = datetime.utcnow()
        await session.commit()

# ❌ WRONG: Hard delete
async def delete(self, material_id: UUID) -> None:
    stmt = delete(MaterialModel).where(MaterialModel.id == material_id)
    await session.execute(stmt)  # ← Destroys data, no audit trail
```

