## Alembic Migrations

**Schema changes use Alembic. Never modify database directly.**

### Create Migration

```bash
# Modify model in code, then:
alembic revision --autogenerate -m "add_priority_to_sales_orders"

# Generates: alembic/versions/20261109_add_priority_to_sales_orders.py
```

### Migration File Template

```python
# alembic/versions/20261109_add_priority_to_sales_orders.py
from alembic import op
from sqlalchemy import Column, Integer, Index, ForeignKey

def upgrade():
    op.add_column("sales_orders", Column("priority", Integer, default=0))
    op.create_index(
        "idx_sales_orders_priority",
        "sales_orders",
        ["priority"]
    )

def downgrade():
    op.drop_index("idx_sales_orders_priority", "sales_orders")
    op.drop_column("sales_orders", "priority")
```

### Migration Workflow

```bash
# Check current state
alembic current

# Apply migrations
alembic upgrade head

# Revert one migration
alembic downgrade -1

# Handle merge conflicts (if multiple heads)
alembic heads                    # Show all heads
alembic merge heads -m "merge description"
alembic upgrade head
```

